      "cwe_id": "CWE-639",
      "explanation": "The endpoint fetches an order by a user-controlled `order_id` without verifying that the authenticated user owns the order. This allows any authenticated user to access any order (IDOR).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "app/routes/orders.py",
          "lines": [
            57,
            64
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "@orders_bp.route(\"/<int:order_id>\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n@require_auth\ndef get_order(order_id: int):\n    \"\"\"Fetch a single order by id.\"\"\"\n    session = get_session()\n    order = session.get(Order, order_id)\n    if order is None:\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"not found\"}), 404\n    return jsonify(order.to_dict())",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Add an ownership check to ensure the authenticated user is the owner of the order before returning it, e.g., `if order.user_id != current_user.id: return jsonify({\"error\": \"forbidden\"}), 403`.",
